# Build context for the Dockerfile at the repo root (01-architecture.md §4.2).
#
# The build stage runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and a full workspace
# build, so the context must carry the sources, every package.json, and the
# lockfile — but nothing that is regenerated inside the image or irrelevant to
# it. Anything host-built that leaks in is worse than useless: host node_modules
# would shadow the install and carry darwin/arm64 native binaries into a linux
# image.

# Installed and built inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Generated at build time by scripts/bundle-dashboard.mjs.
apps/server/dashboard

# VCS + CI metadata: not needed to build the app.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.changeset

# Design comps and the work plan — large, and never part of the image.
# Markdown in general is NOT excluded: it is negligible in size, and a blanket
# `**/*.md` rule would silently break any build input that ever reads one.
workplan
designs

# Local/editor/test noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
.claude
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
**/*.log

# Never ship host secrets or local state into a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/data
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# Test artefacts.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/storybook-static

# The image itself.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
